                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Well damn.  I guess that \"the best things in life\" aren't always \"free\"...  \n\nOnce upon a time, there was a developer who thought he'd make a game trailer showing fly-overs of his colorful world to hide the god awful controls and gameplay.  Once upon a time, he figured this would be a great idea to advertise a future installment of his game.  \n\nSadly, we can see quickly why this game is \"free\"...  Don't let the fly-overs of the game in the trailer fool you.  The controls are horrible and awfully frustrating, and in a game like this where precision is important because interactable items require pixel perfect spotting of your avatar.  Yes, you can hold SHIFT to walk instead of the default run, but it still plays and feels sloppy at best.\n\nWhen a game frustrates you in the first ten minutes, that's NOT a 'good thing\".  While it's a valiant attempt at making the next \"Uncharted\", it needs a LOT of work, and when the price tag is zero, I have my doubts that the developer will ever devote the time needed to make this a game worthy of playing.  There's just too many \"good games\" with responsive and controls which feel good to spend time fighting the game every step of the way in this.\n\nAdd to this, the game completlely fails to ever load a saved game, always getting stuck forever at 90%, forcing you to start the game over completely adds to the frustrations.\n\nNoble attempt like I say, but I can't recommend this, even with a free price tag.  Twiddling your thumbs would be as exciting and way less frustating.",
